<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90361" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσχᾰρ-ίζομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gratify</i> or <i>satisfy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ γαστρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					13.9
				</span></i>
			; <i>stretch a point in</i> one's <i>favour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1141.30
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMeretr.</u>
				9.5
			</span></i>; <i>concede the truth of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς Θετταλοῖς μυθώδεις λόγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					7.7.12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>gratify besides</i>, Ath.Naucr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.211b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>sacrifice</i> something <i>for the sake of</i> something, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πτερυγωμάτων τι τῇ μήτρᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.89
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
